## [0.1.1] — Correctness fixes found during verification

### Fixed: hero H1 rendered invisible
`globals.css` reveals masked lines with `.is-in > .line-mask > span`, which
requires `is-in` on the **direct** parent. The hero had it on an ancestor two
levels up, so the H1 stayed translated 108% down inside its own overflow clip.

Rather than just move the class, the hero's entrance was converted from
IntersectionObserver transitions to plain CSS animations (`.rise-auto`,
`.line-mask.auto`, keyframes `rise-in` / `line-up`). Above-the-fold content now
paints and animates without waiting on hydration, which keeps the H1 — the
likely LCP element — off the JS critical path. `useInView` was dropped from
`Hero.tsx` entirely.

### Fixed: clip-path wipes could never trigger themselves
`clip-path` participates in IntersectionObserver's intersection computation, so
a `.wipe` element clipped to `inset(0 0 100% 0)` reports `intersectionRatio: 0`
forever and can never observe its own entrance. The FAQ accordion and the
closing CTA were both permanently invisible because of this; the hardware table
happened to survive only because its observer sat on an unclipped parent.

Fix: the observer never watches the clipped element. `Reveal`'s `wipe` variant
now renders an unclipped wrapper that holds the ref, with the clip on a child,
and `ClosingCta` does the same.

Hardened `useInView` at the same time:
- default threshold `0.16` -> `0.05`, rootMargin `-8%` -> `-10%`, which is far
  more reliable for tall elements than a ratio threshold
- added a "scrolled past" branch: if an element's bottom is already above the
  viewport it is treated as in view, so a restored scroll position or a fast
  fling can never strand content in its hidden pre-reveal state

### Fixed: two call buttons rendered in the header on mobile
The header rendered a wide button (`hidden sm:inline-flex`) and a compact one
(`sm:hidden`). Passing `hidden` collided with `CallButton`'s own base
`inline-flex`: both are `display` utilities, and stylesheet order decided the
winner, so the "hidden" button stayed visible and both overflowed at 320px.

Fix: one button. `showNumber` already hides the digits below `sm`, so a single
`<CallButton label="Call" showNumber />` gives "Call" on mobile and
"Call (888) 000-0000" from `sm` up. Also added `whitespace-nowrap` to the
wordmark and shrank the disclosure bar type at mobile sizes so it stays on one
line inside the fixed 2.25rem strip.

### Fixed: "starting at" price was quoting a TV add-on
`startingPrice` took the minimum across *all* plans, which is the $10 Stream TV
/ Home Phone add-on — so the closing CTA read "Fiber from $10/mo" and the meta
description matched. Both are internet claims, and neither add-on is sold
without an internet plan.

`startingPrice` and the hero's speed range are now scoped to the `fiber` line.
The site reads $30/mo, which is also the figure altafiber publishes.

### Fixed: footer top row had five children in a four-column grid
The "Details" column wrapped onto a second row. Grid widened to five columns
with a two-column intermediate at `sm`.

### Polish
- Black-hole core moved from 68%/50% to 72%/78% on wide screens; it previously
  sat behind the availability card. Particle density raised (1 per 4200 px²,
  cap 280).
- Hardware cost pills set to `whitespace-nowrap`, with `$99.99/visit` and
  `Ask on call` replacing the longer strings that wrapped inside the pill.

### Hardened: rates and fees centralised further
Bundle feature lists quoted component prices as literal strings
(`"1 Gig symmetrical fiber — $50"`), so a price change updated the cards but
left the bundle line items stale. Introduced exported `RATE` and `FEE` objects
at the top of `lib/content.ts`; plan prices, bundle line items, the hardware
grid and the FAQ answers all read from them.

