## [0.2.0] — Production readiness

### Added: the four policy pages the footer was already linking to
The footer shipped links to `/privacy`, `/terms`, `/accessibility` and
`/do-not-sell`, and none of those routes existed — four dead links, and a
reachable privacy policy is a Google Ads requirement for a landing page that
drives calls.

- `lib/legal.ts` holds the prose as structured `LegalDoc` data and imports
  `site` from `lib/content.ts`, so the entity name, contact address, mailing
  address, governing law and effective date resolve from one place.
- `components/sections/LegalPage.tsx` renders any `LegalDoc` with the site's
  own chrome: navy masthead, prose column, an "Other policies" aside and a
  call CTA.
- Four thin route files under `app/`, each exporting metadata derived from its
  document.

New `site` placeholders, all of which need real values before launch:
`url`, `legalEntity`, `contactEmail`, `mailingAddress`, `policyEffectiveDate`,
`governingLaw`.

The privacy policy states plainly that the ZIP field is processed in the
browser and transmits nothing — which is what the code actually does, and is
worth saying rather than boilerplating around.

**Note on the "no date stamps" constraint:** that rule targeted
"Pricing observed [Date]" strings on the marketing page, and the marketing page
still carries no date of any kind. The policy pages carry a conventional
"Effective" date, because a privacy policy without one is incomplete. It is a
placeholder in `site.policyEffectiveDate` and renders only on those four pages.

### Added: 404, icon, robots, sitemap, structured data
- `app/not-found.tsx` — 404 in the site's own chrome with a route back and a
  call CTA, `robots: noindex`.
- `app/icon.svg` — the wordmark's fiber-strand glyph on altafiber navy.
- `app/robots.ts` and `app/sitemap.ts` — the sitemap is generated from
  `legalDocs`, so adding a policy page adds its entry.
- `components/StructuredData.tsx` — a schema.org `@graph` with `Organization`,
  `WebSite`, `Service`, `OfferCatalog` and `FAQPage`, generated entirely from
  `lib/content.ts`. Search engines penalise structured data that disagrees with
  the visible page, and deriving both from one source makes that impossible.
  Plans with no published rate emit no `price`, so the markup never asserts a
  number the page is not showing.
- `metadataBase` + canonical on the layout so OG and canonical URLs resolve
  absolutely.

### Fixed: WCAG AA contrast failures across nine text styles

A first contrast pass reported zero failures. That result was wrong twice over
and is worth recording so the mistake is not repeated:

1. **The colour parser was broken.** Tailwind v4 emits `oklab(...)`, not
   `rgb(...)`. A naive `match(/[\d.]+/g)` read `oklab(0.999 0.00004 0.00002 /
   0.45)` as `r=0.999, g=0.00004, b=0.00002` — near-black instead of white —
   and reported white-on-navy footer links at 1.05:1. The fix was to stop
   parsing colours by hand and let the browser resolve them: paint the
   background stack and then the text colour onto a 1×1 canvas and read the
   pixel back. That handles `oklab`, alpha compositing and every other colour
   space correctly.
2. **The viewport was collapsed.** The re-run then reported 116 nodes and zero
   failures, but the pane had zero width, so three quarters of the page had
   zero-size rects and was silently skipped. With an explicit 1280×900
   viewport the same audit walked 392 nodes and found nine failing styles.

Measured floors against the real brand backgrounds:

| Foreground on background | Minimum that passes |
|---|---|
| `charcoal` on white | full strength (7.89:1) — `/75` is only 4.13 |
| `charcoal` on `lightest-gray` | full strength (7.32:1) — `/80` is 4.44 |
| `white` on `navy` | `/50` (4.89:1) — `/45` is 4.22, `/40` is 3.63 |
| `white` on `velvet` | `/45` (4.53:1) — `/40` is 3.82 |

Applied across nine files: every `text-charcoal/55…/80` went to full strength,
and every `text-white/40` and `/45` went to `/60`. The plan-card terms strip
moved from `text-charcoal/80` to `text-charcoal` for the same reason.

### Verified (all with an explicit viewport this time)

| Check | Result |
|---|---|
| `next build` | passes, 9 routes prerendered static |
| `tsc --noEmit` | clean |
| Contrast, `/` | 392 text nodes, **0 failures**, lowest 4.51:1 |
| Contrast, `/terms` | 86 text nodes, **0 failures**, lowest 5.37:1 |
| Headings | one `h1` per page, no level jumps |
| Accessible names | 0 interactive elements without one; 0 unlabelled form controls |
| Landmarks | header / main / footer present, all 5 `nav`s labelled |
| Decorative SVG | all hidden from assistive tech (directly or via an `aria-hidden` ancestor) |
| `prefers-reduced-motion` | 6-rule override block confirmed present in the shipped CSS, covering `.reveal`, `.wipe`, `.line-mask`, `.tilt-card`, `.magnetic` and `.rise-auto` |
| Horizontal overflow at 320px | none on `/`, `/privacy` or the 404 |
| Routes | all 200; unknown path returns 404 |
| JSON-LD | parses; 5 entities, 11 offers, 8 FAQ entries; **0 offers whose price is not visible on the page**; no unpriced plan asserted as an offer |
| `tel:` links | 25 on `/`, 3 on the 404, all carrying `data-call-cta` |
| CTA labels | 19 "Call to order", 4 "Call for pricing", no raw number outside header/footer |
| Forbidden strings | 0 |
| Price/speed/fee literals in TSX | 0 |

### Removed
`motion` was installed but never imported — the animation layer is hand-rolled.
Dropped the dependency and the matching `optimizePackageImports` entry. Runtime
dependencies are now `next`, `react`, `react-dom` and `lenis`.

