## [0.3.0] — Hero redesign (client request)

Three changes requested: drop the background animation, drop the hero call
button, and rework the composition — it read as a generic template.

### Removed: the animated hero background
`fx/FiberField.tsx` (the black-hole canvas) is no longer mounted. The hero
background is now entirely static: two radial washes plus a fine 88px grid
masked to fade at the edges. Nothing in the hero background animates, and the
rAF loop is gone from the page entirely.

The component file is kept intact rather than deleted — there is no git history
here to recover it from, and it is a working piece of work. Its header comment
now says it is unmounted and how to drop it into the `#why` section, which is
also navy, if an animated backdrop is wanted somewhere.

**This leaves a brief requirement unmet.** The original spec asked for a black
hole / fiber-optic background animation "in the Hero or technology section".
It is now in neither. Relocating it to `#why` would satisfy the spec without
putting it back in the hero.

### Removed: the hero call button
The standalone "Call to order" CTA beside the price anchor is gone. This
reverses the brief's explicit "KEEP Hero Call Button" rule at the client's
direction.

The "Call to order" **inside the ZIP result panel** was kept. It only appears
after a valid ZIP is submitted, and without it a successful availability check
dead-ends with no way to convert. Page totals moved from 19 "Call to order" /
25 `data-call-cta` to 18 / 24 — exactly one button removed.

The ZIP checker is now the hero's only resting action, so it was promoted from
a field inside a card to a full-width bar: 3.5rem tall, squared, with a solid
alta-green submit.

### Reworked: composition
What made the old hero generic was the stack every SaaS landing page uses — a
pill eyebrow, a gradient headline, a paragraph, buttons, pill chips, and a
floating glassmorphic card on the right. Each of those was replaced with
something that carries information rather than decoration:

| Was | Now |
|---|---|
| Pill eyebrow with a pulsing dot | Rule + uppercase label, masthead-style |
| Tri-colour gradient headline | Solid alta-green second line |
| Glassmorphic card holding a ZIP field | **The fiber ladder** — a bordered data panel |
| Pill trust chips | Rule-marked inline row |
| Animated canvas backdrop | Static grid + radial washes |

**The fiber ladder** is the new centrepiece and the reason the hero is no
longer a template. It draws altafiber's five fiber tiers as proportional bars
on a log scale — log, because 100 Mbps against 6 Gig on a linear scale
collapses the low tier to a sliver; the bar is floored at 14% so it still reads
as a bar. The lead plan is highlighted in alta-green and carries the
`<PriceLockup />` price anchor above the list. Every tier, speed, price and
badge comes from `plansByLine("fiber")`, so adding or repricing a tier in
`lib/content.ts` redraws the ladder with no layout edit.

### Two bugs caught in review of the first pass
- **The ladder scale was wrong.** The lead plan's Down/Up bars sat in a panel
  that was wider than the ladder's bar column, so 1 Gig at 62% of a wide track
  rendered visibly *longer* than 6 Gig at 100% of a narrow one — the chart said
  the opposite of the truth. Fixed by putting all five tiers in one list with a
  single shared bar column; the separate Down/Up bars were dropped and the
  symmetry claim is carried by the panel header and the lead plan's
  "1 Gig down · 1 Gig up" line.
- **The trust row stranded a divider.** Separators were rendered before every
  item except the first, so when the row wrapped, a divider landed at the start
  of the second line. Replaced with a uniform leading green rule on every item,
  which is wrap-safe.

### Verified
| Check | Result |
|---|---|
| `next build` | passes, 9 routes static |
| `tsc --noEmit` | clean |
| `<canvas>` in hero | 0 |
| `tel:` links in hero at rest | 0 |
| Price anchor + ZIP checker in hero | both present |
| Remaining hero animation | one-shot entrance reveals + the trust ticker only |
| Contrast, `/` | 401 nodes, **0 failures**, lowest 4.74:1 |
| Horizontal overflow at 320px | none |
| `tel:` links page-wide | 24, all with `data-call-cta` |
| CTA labels | 18 "Call to order", 4 "Call for pricing" |
| Forbidden strings | 0 |
| Price/speed literals in TSX | 0 |

