## [0.4.0] — Light theme, brand alignment, copy pass

Client supplied screenshots of altafiber.com and asked the site to match it
exactly, with no dark theme; plus a copy pass, a new hero panel, removal of the
network diagram, and a rename.

### Converted: dark theme -> altafiber's light theme
altafiber.com is a white site — black headings, bright-blue accents and CTAs,
pale grey alternating bands, one dark gradient band, and a dark navy footer.
The build now mirrors that.

Added semantic roles to `@theme` rather than scattering raw hexes, so
components state intent. All values are the official brand tokens already
extracted from altafiber's stylesheet:

| Role | Token | Hex |
|---|---|---|
| `ink` | velvet-black | `#101014` — headings |
| `body` | charcoal-gray | `#515156` — body copy |
| `accent` | dark-blue | `#005bb5` — CTAs and links |
| `accent-bright` | fiber-blue | `#4294f7` — large accents, rules, motif |
| `surface` | white | `#ffffff` |
| `surface-alt` | lightest-gray | `#f6f6fa` — alternating bands |
| `tint` | lightest-fiber-blue | `#edf5ff` — pale fills |
| `line` | light-gray | `#ebebed` — hairlines |

`accent` is the CTA colour rather than `accent-bright` because white on
`#4294f7` is only 2.9:1, while white on `#005bb5` is 7.0:1.

**Two surfaces are deliberately still dark, because altafiber's own site has
them:** the "Why 100% fiber internet" band is a black-to-blue gradient exactly
as on altafiber.com, and the footer is altafiber navy. Everything else is white
or pale grey.

### Added: the altafiber strand motif
`fx/BrandWaves.tsx` reproduces altafiber's signature bundle of thin curved
lines. It replaces `fx/FiberPaths.tsx` (deleted — strictly superseded) and
carries the SVG path-draw animation: each strand draws itself in on entry.
Used behind the hero and the plans section.

### Rebuilt: the hero right panel
The fiber ladder was replaced with a single premium plan card — offer ribbon,
symmetrical download/upload read-out, `<PriceLockup />`, four inclusions, and a
"Compare all plans" anchor (not a call button; the hero still has none). Every
value resolves from `leadPlan`.

### Removed: the scroll-scrubbed network diagram
`GatewayAssembly` is no longer mounted in "How it works", which is now a clean
three-across step layout with a connecting rule. **This drops the brief's
scroll-scrubbed assembly animation requirement** — flagged, not forgotten.

### Copy pass
| Before | After |
|---|---|
| Future-proof fiber internet for your home. | 100% fiber internet, built for your home. |
| Symmetrical fiber, straight to the house | Symmetrical speeds on every fiber plan |
| Add TV or Home Phone and pay less for both | Bundle internet with TV or Home Phone |
| Live TV and streaming in one place | Live television and streaming, unified |
| A home line built on the same fiber drop | Reliable home phone service |
| Hardware, fees and what is actually included | Equipment, fees and inclusions |
| Three steps, one phone call | Three steps to getting connected |
| What changes the day it goes in | Why 100% fiber internet |

Section sublines were rewritten to match. The fiber subline no longer mentions
ordering by phone, per the request.

### Renamed: Fiber Direct -> altafiber
`site.retailer` is now "altafiber", so every visible name — wordmark, metadata,
footer, all four policy pages — follows from that one field. The wordmark is
set as altafiber sets it: "alta" in ink, "fiber" in brand blue.

**`site.legalEntity` was deliberately NOT renamed.** An authorized retailer
cannot present itself as the carrier — that is a misrepresentation risk under
Google Ads policy and a legal exposure. It is now the placeholder
`[Legal entity name]` so the policy pages name the real operating company. The
"Independent Authorized Retailer of altafiber" disclosure bar remains sticky
and non-dismissable.

### Three bugs caught in review
- **Hydration mismatch in `BrandWaves`.** Full-precision floats serialise
  differently on server and client (`0.6724900435477166` vs `…167`), which
  React reported as a mismatch on every strand. Fixed by rounding
  `strokeOpacity` to 3dp and every path coordinate to 2dp. Verified: 0 values
  with 5+ decimals in the SSR output, and a clean console on a fresh server.
- **Featured plan cards rendered invisible prices.** `PlanCard` passed
  `invert={featured}` to `<PriceLockup />`. Featured cards became white in this
  pass, so that meant white text on white — 4 prices at 1.0:1 contrast. The
  lockup no longer inverts.
- **The wordmark failed AA.** `#4294f7` on white is 3.08:1, fine for the 58px
  H1 accent (needs 3.0) but not for 17px live text (needs 4.5). The wordmark's
  "fiber" moved to `accent` at 7.0:1. A logo *image* would be exempt; live text
  is not.

### Verified
| Check | Result |
|---|---|
| `next build` | passes, 9 routes static |
| `tsc --noEmit` | clean |
| Console on fresh load | **no errors**, hydration mismatch gone |
| Contrast, `/` | 397 nodes, **0 failures**; lowest 3.08:1 is the 58px H1 accent, which needs 3.0 |
| Page background | white; only the "Why fiber" gradient band and footer are dark, as on altafiber.com |
| Network diagram | removed — 0 diagram SVGs, no residual copy |
| `<canvas>` | 0 page-wide |
| "Fiber Direct" | 0 occurrences |
| Horizontal overflow at 320px | none on `/` or `/privacy` |
| `tel:` links | 23, all with `data-call-cta` |
| CTA labels | 17 "Call to order", 4 "Call for pricing" |
| Price/speed literals in TSX | 0 |

