## [0.8.1] — Hero white wash reduced further

Gradient pulled back so more of the photograph shows:

| | before | after |
|---|---|---|
| solid white to | 42% | **32%** |
| ~0.9 opacity to | 54% | **47%** |
| fully clear from | 88% | **79%** |

The constraint is that the type column ends near 50% of the viewport, so the
ramp still holds roughly 0.85 opacity there. Checked against the darkest pixel
actually behind that point — sampled from the source file at x=50%,
`rgb(30,16,5)` — body copy lands at **5.73:1**, above the 4.5 floor.

Verified with the paint-order probe: 386 nodes, **0 failures**. Hero body copy
measures 7.89:1 at element centre (which sits in the solid-white region); the
5.73:1 figure above is the worst case at the right edge of the text, where the
ramp has begun.

