## [0.9.0] — Ambient motion

### Hero
- **Slow drift on the photograph** (`.hero-drift`) — 32s, scale 1.02 → 1.09
  with a slight translate, alternating. Starts at 1.02 so no edge can be
  revealed as it moves.
- **Eyebrow rule draws itself out** from the left on load.
- **Ambient colour wash** behind the copy, confined to the white side.

### Other sections
`components/fx/AmbientWash.tsx` — three oversized radial-gradient blobs in the
brand palette drifting on long independent cycles (34s / 44s / 38s), so the
pattern never visibly repeats. Applied to the light sections: fiber, bundles,
phone, hardware and FAQ. The TV and "How it works" sections run on photographs
and are left alone.

**Performance:** every animation here moves `transform` only — no `filter`, no
`background-position`, no width/height — so it all stays on the compositor and
costs no layout or paint. Softness comes from the gradient stops rather than a
blur filter, which would be expensive to animate continuously. All of it is
switched off under `prefers-reduced-motion`.

Blobs sit inside an `overflow-hidden` wrapper, so the oversized circles and
their negative insets cannot create page overflow — confirmed at 320px.

### A real regression, caught and fixed
The probe was extended to evaluate **radial** gradients (interpolating by
distance from the blob centre) as well as linear ones. With that in place it
found a genuine failure the previous version could not see:

The hero headline accent was `fiber-blue #4294f7`, which is 3.08:1 on white —
a technical pass for large text but with no headroom. The blue ambient wash
tints the backdrop blue behind blue text, dragging it to **2.85:1**, under the
3.0 floor.

Two fixes rather than one, so it cannot recur:
- Added a `--color-headline-accent: #2b82ed` token (3.81:1 on white) used only
  for the hero headline. `accent-bright` stays as-is for rules and dots, which
  are decorative and not subject to text contrast.
- Gave the hero a half-strength `subtle` wash tone, since that is the one place
  a large blue headline sits over the wash.

Lowest ratio on the page is now **3.74:1**, better headroom than the 3.08
it had before this change.

### Verified
| Check | Result |
|---|---|
| `next build` | passes |
| `tsc --noEmit` | clean |
| Ambient washes | 18 blobs across hero + 5 light sections, all animating |
| Contrast, `/` (probe now handles radial gradients) | 386 nodes, **0 failures**, lowest 3.74:1 |
| Horizontal overflow at 320px | none; all blobs confirmed inside `overflow-hidden` |
| `prefers-reduced-motion` | `.hero-drift`, `.ambient-blob` and `.rule-draw` all explicitly disabled |

